\section{Overview}

This is a native C++ reimplementation of the Berzerk game logic. Instead of
emulating Z80 instructions, it implements the game algorithms directly in C++,
using the Phase 6 disassembly documentation as the blueprint.

The native implementation operates on the same memory model as the emulator:
VRAM (8~KB), Work RAM (1~KB), Color RAM (2~KB), and Magic RAM (74181 ALU).
All sprite drawing goes through the same [[magic\_ram\_write]] pipeline, so
pixel-level output must match the emulator exactly.

Verification is performed by the Phase 7 cosimulation harness, which compares
VRAM content at frame boundaries.

