\subsection{Lives Display}

Reimplementation of the lives display at \$259A--\$25BD. Draws
(deaths$-$1) stick-man icons (character \$80) at the bottom of the screen.

<<native draw lives>>=
void BerzerkNative::draw_lives()
{
    // Determine position based on current player
    uint8_t y = 0xD5;
    uint8_t x = (m_state.current_player == 2) ? 0xE8 : 0x38;

    // Set magic RAM control: mode 0, shift from X
    uint8_t shift = x & 0x07;
    m_video.magic.control = shift;
    m_video.magic.last_shift_data = 0;
    m_video.magic.intercept = 1;

    uint16_t dest = calc_magic_ram_addr(y, x);

    int lives_to_draw = m_state.deaths - 1;
    if (lives_to_draw <= 0) return;

    for (int i = 0; i < lives_to_draw; i++) {
        print_char(0x80, dest);
        dest++;  // next character position
    }
}
@

\subsection{Colour Fill}

Reimplementation of COLOUR\_FILL at \$3657. Fills a rectangle in colour RAM.
For upright cabinet: base address is \$8100 + offset.

<<native colour fill>>=
void BerzerkNative::colour_fill(uint16_t offset, uint8_t lines,
                                 uint8_t width, uint8_t colour)
{
    // Upright cabinet: colour RAM at $8100 + offset
    uint16_t base = 0x0100 + offset;  // index into color_ram ($8000 base)

    for (int row = 0; row < lines; row++) {
        for (int col = 0; col < width; col++) {
            uint16_t idx = (base + col) & 0x07FF;
            m_video.color_ram[idx] = colour;
        }
        base += 0x20;  // next row (32 bytes per row)
    }
}
@

\subsection{Post-Maze Rendering}

After maze generation, the Z80 code at \$2597--\$25C9 sets up colour
attributes, draws life icons, and displays the score.

<<native post maze render>>=
void BerzerkNative::post_maze_render()
{
    // $2597: call $369F -- status area colour fill
    colour_fill(0x0680, 4, 0x20, 0x77);

    // $36A7: call $35E7 -- additional colour regions
    colour_fill(0x0680, 4, 0x0A, 0xAA);
    colour_fill(0x0696, 4, 0x0A, 0xDD);

    // $259A: draw lives
    draw_lives();

    // $25C6: show score
    show_score();
}
